# v108 cadence rollback/hybrid: v90-like native QWidget update coalescing is default; custom sparse/vsync schedulers remain A/B.
# During active lyric animation cyclic GC is deferred between sessions, and rows with no actual audio-scaled glyphs use the plain v90 cursor fast path.
# v1.8.9.63 NetEase Bridge finalization / legacy-cleanup stage 2: the plugin caches the
# last native currentTime so a mid-song paused cold start can bind without UIA, playing
# heartbeat grace prevents normal next-track handoff from waking Chromium/UIA, and Bridge
# render diagnostics now report the effective zero provider preroll instead of stale state.
# v70 follow-up: seek visual state is timeline-clean, NetEase native YRC/KLYRIC is never
# replaced merely for finer third-party granularity, max-visible residency is capacity-driven,
# long-gap cleanup waits for >=12s real silence and exits near the next row, and placement
# metrics/current-to-history glyph caches avoid repeated decorative-font work. QQ timing remains unchanged.
# v71 layout guard: fix the v70 placement metric refactor typo that left guard_pad undefined
# once history/obstacle avoidance became active. A narrow fallback prevents future placement
# exceptions from reusing the previous lyric coordinates and visually stacking every row.
# v72 comfort-clock pass: keep provider token gaps, but stop applying the Western-friendly
# +120ms NetEase Bridge anticipation to CJK syllable clocks. CJK precise rows use a near-zero
# render phase, while weak/large-phase Japanese/Chinese/Korean cross-provider KRC falls back
# to native ordinary LRC instead of forcing a foreign clock onto the current audio.
# v73 render audit: preserve v72 timing, seek, residency, placement, and live-history motion.
# Only the expensive styled-glyph raster stage is cached in a bounded shared LRU; position,
# per-character shake, reveal opacity, perspective, capacity hold, and fade timing stay dynamic.
# v74 seek lifecycle correction: an NCM cross-line seek fades only the interrupted visible
# current prefix. Held history and already-exiting rows stay alive; capacity eviction is reserved
# for the next normal completed-row transition. Fade-lane safety is separated from history
# capacity enforcement. Raster fallback is also hardened against null/non-space glyph results.
# v75 crisp-clock audit: cache only glow/shadow while the glyph face stays vector-sharp;
# Bridge seek phase is direct and script classification comes from raw currentTime. A close-duration
# KRC large phase may be globally corrected only when many matching rows agree with low spread.
# v76 vector-live/trust audit: retained/fading rows batch cached glyph outlines into one vector path;
# shake targets keep the user cadence while motion interpolates smoothly. NetEase precise Bridge uses one
# small uniform source-faithful phase, Bridge handoff reanchors without fake seek trails, and foreign KRC
# must have a trustworthy native-LRC timing anchor before it can drive precise rendering.
# v77 native-first source convergence: NetEase now exhausts its own current-ID clock first, then may use a
# strictly matched *alternate NetEase* YRC/KLYRIC before probing Kugou. Any non-current clock is only an
# enhancement: native ordinary LRC remains the reference, robust anchor drift is checked, unverified foreign
# clocks are never cached, and final source selection is logged explicitly. QQ keeps native QRC-first defaults.
# v81 QQ authority audit: keep the mature v47 hover/gesture state machine, but close its cold-start hole:
# a QQ mm:ss Text pair cannot become the initial anchor or duration pre-calibration merely by repeating.
# It must prove real wall-clock-like forward progression while playing. Native QRC keeps the mature fixed QQ baseline
# phase instead of stacking the later cadence-dependent 180-308ms row-by-row look-ahead.
# v85 sync consolidation: QQ phase calibration/seek carry sample only validated mm:ss +1s edges;
# NetEase Bridge ownership retires stale UIA seek candidates without deleting fallback code;
# NetEase alternate/KRC enhancement probes may overlap to reduce cold track-switch search latency.
# v82 native phase / QQ seek guard: add same-song native YRC/LRC diagnostics, mature QQ seek-phase carry,
# and a non-progress-click fast path for lyric-page seeks while keeping rail-hover quarantine.
# v83 arbitration follow-up: native YRC/LRC self-delta is diagnostic only; a very large coherent delta revokes
# automatic native-word-clock authority and reuses the verified enhancement/native-LRC arbitration. QQ non-rail
# clicks are edge-deduplicated, and cursor-off-rail wall-clock-like two-point seeks may confirm in ~1s.
# v1.8.9.115: keep v114 QQ lyric-page guard and all timing behavior; smooth the visual cadence
# v1.8.9.121: Kugou seek gestures are captured by a dedicated Windows WH_MOUSE_LL hook.
# Short drags are queued losslessly and consumed on the normal snapshot path, so UIA polling can
# no longer make the app miss a quick custom-drawn progress-rail drag. First-drag diagnostics log
# normalized coordinates even when rejected. Dense custom-UI discovery is background/low-frequency.
# v1.8.9.120: Kugou provisional clock becomes interaction-tracked. Dense UI discovery is
# throttled out of the 200ms transport cadence; scan time is compensated instead of becoming
# a permanent opening delay. Explicit bottom-rail drags may re-anchor the local clock and teach
# a rail Y for later clicks, while logs keep `real_clock=0` until a genuine player timeline is
# discovered. QQ v116 phase behavior and the NetEase internal Bridge stay unchanged.
# v1.8.9.116: make QQ phase correction frame/UIA-latency independent. Whole-second Text
# publication time is allowed to jitter inside its natural 1s bucket; only a real bucket
# corridor violation may steer the monotonic lyric clock or trigger post-seek rephase.
# interaction. Text matches are hints only until the validated compact playback clock
# confirms an actual seek; opening/closing the lyric page can no longer seize the visual
# clock merely because the page header matches a timestamped metadata row.
